---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import provenance from '../../../data-pipeline/data/processed/_provenance.json';

const datasets = Object.entries(provenance as Record<string, any>).sort(([a], [b]) => a.localeCompare(b));
const accessed = datasets[0]?.[1]?.accessed ?? '';

const rejected = [
  { name: 'RBI DBIE (data.rbi.org.in)', why: 'An Angular application with no documented public REST API. Net interest margin is derived from filed income statements instead, which is more defensible than screen-scraping a portal.' },
  { name: 'NPCI direct scraping', why: 'npci.org.in returns HTTP 403 to every scripted request. Recent months are transcribed from a browser session with per-row provenance instead. The overlap month matches the open mirror exactly, confirming no level shift at the seam.' },
  { name: 'data.gov.in', why: 'The public sandbox key authenticates, but filtered resource queries time out and many finance resources have no active API. It would add nothing the spine does not already cover.' },
  { name: 'Perspective, Superset, Panel, Redash, Vizro, glue', why: 'Each needs a live Python or Node backend, which a static free-hosted site cannot have, or ships several megabytes of WASM to pivot 36 rows. The workbench is built in code instead, which keeps the page fast.' },
  { name: 'D3', why: 'Dropped after the charts were specified. A four-point cohort chart is server-rendered SVG with no JavaScript at all, and ECharts covers the rest. Removing it took a dependency and a client bundle out of the project.' },
  { name: 'WebGPU', why: 'No dataset here is remotely large enough to justify it.' },
];
---
<Base title="Methodology and sources: India FS Pulse" description="Every dataset, its publisher, coverage and access date, plus what this analysis deliberately does not do.">
  <article class="doc">
    <a class="back" href="/">← India FS Pulse</a>
    <p class="kicker">Method</p>
    <h1>Sources, provenance, and what this analysis cannot know</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every figure on this site is computed by a script from a committed dataset. Nothing is
      typed in by hand. This page is generated from the provenance ledger the fetchers write,
      so it cannot drift from what the pipeline actually pulled.
    </p>

    <h2>Datasets</h2>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Dataset</th><th>Publisher</th><th>Coverage</th><th>Rows</th><th>Terms</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {datasets.map(([name, e]) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{name}</code></td>
              <td><a href={e.url} rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank">{e.publisher}</a></td>
              <td>{e.coverage}</td>
              <td class="num">{Number(e.rows).toLocaleString('en-IN')}</td>
              <td class="terms">{e.licence}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">All accessed {accessed}. Code in this repository is MIT licensed; each dataset retains its publisher's own terms.</p>

    <h2>Caveats carried into every exhibit</h2>
    <ul class="caveats">
      {datasets.filter(([, e]) => e.note).map(([name, e]) => (
        <li><code>{name}</code>, {e.note}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2>What was deliberately not used</h2>
    <dl class="rejected">
      {rejected.map((r) => (<div><dt>{r.name}</dt><dd>{r.why}</dd></div>))}
    </dl>

    <h2>Three rules the pipeline enforces</h2>
    <ol class="rules">
      <li><b>Never fabricate a number.</b> If a value was not fetched or computed it stays a visible gap. Four months NPCI does not publish are left empty rather than interpolated.</li>
      <li><b>Fail loud on shape change.</b> Each fetcher validates its schema and range. The bank fetcher refused to run when a NIM came back negative, correctly, because the company was a payments firm, not a bank.</li>
      <li><b>Synthetic data announces itself.</b> The survey panel is generated. It says so in the filename, on the chart, and at the top of the memo.</li>
    </ol>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc { max-width: 82ch; margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem) var(--gutter) 5rem; }
  .back { color: var(--text-3); font-size: 0.8rem; text-decoration: none; }
  .back:hover { color: var(--signal-text); }
  h1 { font-size: var(--step-3); margin: 0.4rem 0 1rem; }
  h2 { font-size: var(--step-1); margin: 2.6rem 0 0.9rem; padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
       border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .lede { color: var(--text-2); font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; max-width: 66ch; }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.8rem; min-width: 640px; }
  th { text-align: left; color: var(--text-3); font-size: 0.66rem; text-transform: uppercase;
       letter-spacing: 0.06em; padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  td { padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem 0.6rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
       color: var(--text-2); vertical-align: top; }
  td.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .terms { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-3); }
  code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text); }
  a { color: var(--text-2); text-decoration-color: var(--signal-line); }
  .note { color: var(--text-3); font-size: 0.76rem; margin-top: 0.7rem; }
  .caveats { color: var(--text-2); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.65; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  .caveats li { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  .rejected > div { padding: 0.85rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .rejected dt { color: var(--text); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .rejected dd { margin: 0.3rem 0 0; color: var(--text-2); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .rules { color: var(--text-2); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .rules li { margin: 0.6rem 0; }
  .rules b { color: var(--text); }
</style>
